## Summary

Three coordinated fixes to `TriptychImage` (`src/reflection.jsx`), addressing the two failure modes from the previous audit that explain a fully-populated entry rendering blank:

### Fix 1 — Identity check on `src` in the first `useEffect`
`decorate(entry)` returns a **new object every render**, so the `[src, fallbackSrc]` effect was firing on every parent re-render — resetting `activeSrc`, status to `loading`, and revealed to `false`. The reveal animation's opacity-0 stayed visible because status never settled at `ready` long enough to fire the `requestAnimationFrame`.

```diff
+ const lastLoadedSrc = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
+   // Fix 1: identity check on src. If the prop equals the source we already
+   // verified, skip the reset entirely — keeps `status: "ready"` and
+   // `revealed: true` stable across decorate()-induced re-renders.
+   if (src === lastLoadedSrc.current) return;
    setActiveSrc(src || fallbackSrc || null);
    setStatus(src || fallbackSrc ? "loading" : "error");
    setRevealed(false);
  }, [src, fallbackSrc]);
```

`lastLoadedSrc.current` is set inside `img.onload` to the `activeSrc` that successfully loaded.

### Fix 2 — Same identity check in the load effect
If the load effect re-fires (e.g., `fallbackSrc` changed but `activeSrc` is still the value we already loaded), jump straight to `ready` instead of firing a fresh `Image()` probe:

```diff
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!activeSrc) { setStatus("error"); return; }
+   if (activeSrc === lastLoadedSrc.current) {
+     setStatus("ready");
+     return;
+   }
    setStatus("loading");
    const img = new Image();
    img.onload = () => {
+     lastLoadedSrc.current = activeSrc;
      setStatus("ready");
    };
```

### Fix 3 — Render with `<img>` tags instead of CSS `background-image`
Safari silently fails to paint `background-image: url(<huge data URL>)` once the URL exceeds ~32 KB. The `Image()` probe reports `onload` fine, so status reaches `ready` and revealed flips to true — but the three CSS-background divs paint nothing. `<img>` handles large data URLs reliably.

Each panel is now an `overflow: hidden` div containing an `<img>` sized `300% × 100%` with a `left: -i*100%` offset — preserves the exact triptych slicing math from the original `backgroundSize: 300% 100%` / `backgroundPosition` pair:

```jsx
<div role="img" aria-label={alt}
  style={{ display: "flex", width: "100%", aspectRatio: "1560 / 680", overflow: "hidden", background: SURFACE_BG }}>
  {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
    <div key={i} style={{
      flex: 1,
      position: "relative",
      overflow: "hidden",
      opacity: revealed ? 1 : 0,
      transform: revealed ? "translateX(0)" : "translateX(20px)",
      transition: `opacity 400ms ease-out ${i * 150}ms, transform 400ms ease-out ${i * 150}ms`,
      willChange: "opacity, transform",
    }}>
      `&lt;img
        src={activeSrc}
        alt=""
        aria-hidden="true"
        style={{
          position: "absolute",
          top: 0,
          left: `${-i * 100}%`,
          width: "300%",
          height: "100%",
          display: "block",
          pointerEvents: "none",
        }}
      /&gt;`
    </div>
  ))}
</div>
```

Outer container preserves its `aspect-ratio: 1560 / 680`, flex layout, and per-panel reveal animation. Outer ARIA stays `role="img" aria-label={alt}`; inner `<img>` tags carry `alt=""` + `aria-hidden="true"` so screen readers announce the triptych once, not three times.

## Constraints honored
- One file: `src/reflection.jsx`.
- Only `TriptychImage` modified. `GalleryEntry`, `ExpandedEntry`, `refreshSignedUrl`, `urlReachable`, the cleanup effect, the on-load `signedUrls` accumulator — all untouched.
- Render API unchanged (same props: `src`, `fallbackSrc`, `alt`, `placeholderFontSize`, `onError`). Callers don't change.

## Verification
- `npm run build` clean.
- `npm test` 82/82.
- `git diff --stat` → `+46 −5` in one file.

## Test plan
- [ ] Deploy → reload the Reflection tab. A previously-blank current-week entry should now actually paint.
- [ ] Quickly switch tabs / scroll while photos are loading — no more thrash; once a card is painted, it stays painted across re-renders.
- [ ] On a card that genuinely can't load either src or fallback, the "Image unavailable" placeholder still renders and the × button still surfaces (`onError` callback chain unchanged).
- [ ] Inline-only entries (no `url`, only `inline` data URL) now paint reliably in Safari where they previously failed silently.

